Hi Omnia,

Thanks for running the release and for the quick turnaround on the
signing issue.

I did the following to validate RC4:
- Verified the signatures and checksums of the source, binary, site-docs
  and release notes artifacts, and of all the staged Maven artifacts
  (the RC3 signing issue is fixed)
- Checked that the source tarball matches the 4.4.0-rc4 tag
- Built from source and ran the unit tests with JDK 17 and JDK 25
- Ran the quickstart with the binary on JDK 17 and JDK 25, with classic
  and consumer groups
- Did a rolling upgrade of a 3-node combined cluster from 4.3.1 to 4.4.0
  while producing and consuming (classic and consumer groups), then
  upgraded the features with `--release-version 4.4`
- Ran the apache/kafka and apache/kafka-native images
- Built a small producer/consumer/admin app against the staged Maven
  artifacts and ran it with JDK 17 and JDK 25
- Spot checked the release notes, Javadoc and documentation
- Checked the system test results: the two NetworkDegradeTest failures
  fail on ping between the test workers, so they are not related to the
  release

One non-blocking note: the documentation PR
(https://github.com/apache/kafka-site/pull/905) still has the RC1 docs
and references 4.3.0 in the quickstarts, so it needs to be updated
before it is merged.

+1 (binding)

Best,
David

