--000000000000e2a831065e335bdb
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="UTF-8"

I am currently trying to switch my Kafka test install to SSL by using the
guide on the page Encryption and Authentication using SSL, however I am
failing to get anything working including the internal broker
communication, while I have had some experience with using openssl, I have
none using keytool, so I assume that I am missing steps that should be
obvious but are not mentioned in the guide or the guide does not completely
fit to the requirements like it is based on a previous version of Java that
is deprecated now since some steps give an error about unsupported command
parameters.

Is it certain that the guide contains all steps necessary to actually get a
dev installation of Kafka working with SSL?


Thanks in advance,
Alexander

