Hi Alexander,

I also went through the docs and indeed it contains outdated
information which can prevent you from setting up Kafka with SSL. I have
opened KAFKA-21329 <https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-21329> to
work on updating the docs. It likely won't reach the official docs site
until the release of Kafka 4.5 which is still months away. In the meantime
you can check out my patch at kafka/pull/23907
<https://github.com/apache/kafka/pull/23907> and hopefully it can unblock
you in your SSL setup work. Of course any feedback is welcome on the
updated steps :)

Thanks,
Gergely

On Mon, 19 Oct 2026 at 17:43, Alexander Lehmann <alexlehm@gmail.com> wrote:

> I am currently trying to switch my Kafka test install to SSL by using the
> guide on the page Encryption and Authentication using SSL, however I am
> failing to get anything working including the internal broker
> communication, while I have had some experience with using openssl, I have
> none using keytool, so I assume that I am missing steps that should be
> obvious but are not mentioned in the guide or the guide does not completely
> fit to the requirements like it is based on a previous version of Java that
> is deprecated now since some steps give an error about unsupported command
> parameters.
>
> Is it certain that the guide contains all steps necessary to actually get a
> dev installation of Kafka working with SSL?
>
>
> Thanks in advance,
> Alexander
>
> --
> Alexander Lehmann <alexlehm@gmail.com>
> https://links.lehmann.cx/
> https://about.me/alexlehm
>

